  "recording_type": "electrocorticography (subdural ECoG grid; clinical epilepsy monitoring), 500 Hz, stored in microvolts; upper-body pose from video at 30 Hz (pixel coordinates)",
  "verified_at": "2026-11-07",
  "modality": "ecog",
  "line_hz": 60,
  "notes": [
    "Participant sub-07: one 64-electrode grid (group RFGRID; 63 marked good in the file's 'good' column). Chosen a priori: smallest channel count with >= 190 curated reach events on three recording days.",
    "Mains frequency 60 Hz: the stored signal already shows notch dips at 60, 120 and 180 Hz (upstream filtering by the dataset authors), consistent with a US recording site.",
    "Electrode 'location' is 'unknown' for every electrode in the file (hard-coded by the authors' converter); x/y/z are given without a stated coordinate space.",
    "Pose SpatialSeries declare unit 'meters' with conversion NaN; the authors' converter and reach features ('_px') show they are video pixel coordinates. BrainOS reports them as unit 'arbitrary'.",
    "The electrodes table's low_freq_R2 / high_freq_R2 columns come from the authors' prior regression analysis of these recordings; BrainOS never uses them for channel selection (it would leak outcome information).",
    "'Blocklist (Data break)' epochs of 0.03-0.2 s recur about every 2 minutes; samples there are not NaN and are passed through unchanged, but frames overlapping them are flagged dropped_samples and BrainOS's evaluation excludes bins near them."
  ],
